    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35154" root="قتر" body-key="q">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قتّر</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَقْتِيرٌ</span>: see 1. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>He excited,</i> or
<i>raised, the scent termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُتَار</span>. (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قتّر لِلْأَسَدِ</span>
<i>He put for the lion some flesh-meat</i> (S, K) <i>in the
pitfall,</i> (S,) <i>that he might perceive its scent.</i> (S,
K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قتّر لِلْوَحْشِ</span> <i>He</i> (a hunter, TA) <i>fumigated</i>
[<i>himself</i> or <i>his clothes</i>] <i>with camels' dung, in order
that the wild animals might not perceive his</i> (the
hunter's) <i>smell,</i> (K, TA,) <i>and flee from him.</i>
(TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قتّر عَلَى عِيَالِهِ</span>: see 1.

